Author:     Mark Shank <mark.shank@gmail.com>
AuthorDate: Wed Oct 21 11:53:25 2026 -0400
Commit:     Mark Shank <mark.shank@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Wed Oct 21 15:49:56 2026 -0400

    Compute one RoPE table per V4.1 decode token
    
    Every layer computed the same RoPE cos/sin values for the current position, in both the attention and the indexer. Decode now computes them once per token into a small table at the start of the step, and the layers read it.
    
    With the table, the kernel that finishes attention can also undo the RoPE rotation and round to bf16 as it writes its output, so the next projection becomes a plain Q8_0 matrix-vector product. In the indexer, applying RoPE and quantizing the query to FP4 are now one kernel instead of two. The results are bit-identical.
    
    DS4_METAL_DISABLE_V41_ROPE_TABLE=1 computes RoPE in each layer as before.

